ide: ignoring susceptibility is not &#x02018;good science&#x02019;</article-title><source>Environ Toxicol Pharmacol</source><volume>4</volume><fpage>219</fpage><lpage>228</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">21781824</pub-id></element-citation></ref><ref id="b11-ehp0115-000743"><element-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group><name><surname>Finkel</surname><given-names>AM</given-names></name></person-group><year>1990</year><article-title>A simple formula for calculating the mass density of a lognormally distributed characteristic&#x02014;applications to risk analysis</article-title><source>Risk Anal</source><volume>10</volume><fpage>291</fpage><lpage>301</lpage></element-citation></ref><ref id="b12-ehp0115-000743"><element-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group><name><surname>Jacobson</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Hengartner</surname><given-names>NW</given-names></name><name><surname>Louis</surname><given-names>TA</given-names></name></person-group><year>2005</year><article-title>Inequity measures for evaluations of environmental justice: a case study of close proximity to highways in NYC</article-title><source>Environ Plan A</source><volume>37</volume><fpage>21</fpage><lpage>43</lpage></element-citation></ref><ref id="b13-ehp0115-000743"><element-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group><name><surname>Kawachi</surname><given-names>I</given-names></name><name><surname>Kennedy</surname><given-names>BP</given-names></name></person-group><year>1997</year><article-title>The relationship of income inequality to mortality: does the choice of indicator matter?</article-title><source>Soc Sci Med</source><volume>45</volume><fpage>1121</fpage><lpage>1127</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9257403</pub-id></element-citation></ref><ref id="b14-ehp0115-000743"><element-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group><name><surname>Levy</surname><given-names>JI</given-names></name><name><surname>Chemerynski</surname><given-