Environ Health Perspect</source><volume>110</volume><issue>suppl 2</issue><fpage>289</fpage><lpage>295</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11929740</pub-id></element-citation></ref><ref id="b18-ehp0115-000743"><element-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group><name><surname>Macinko</surname><given-names>JA</given-names></name><name><surname>Starfield</surname><given-names>B</given-names></name></person-group><year>2002</year><article-title>Annotated bibliography on equity in health, 1980&#x02013;2001</article-title><source>Int J Equity Health</source><volume>1</volume><fpage>1</fpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12234390</pub-id></element-citation></ref><ref id="b19-ehp0115-000743"><element-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group><name><surname>Millimet</surname><given-names>DL</given-names></name><name><surname>Slottje</surname><given-names>D</given-names></name></person-group><year>2002a</year><article-title>An environmental Paglin-Gini</article-title><source>Appl Econ Lett</source><volume>9</volume><fpage>271</fpage><lpage>274</lpage></element-citation></ref><ref id="b20-ehp0115-000743"><element-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group><name><surname>Millimet</surname><given-names>DL</given-names></name><name><surname>Slottje</surname><given-names>D</given-names></name></person-group><year>2002b</year><article-title>Environmental compliance costs and the distribution of emissions in the U.S</article-title><source>J Reg Sci</source><volume>42</volume><fpage>87</fpage><lpage>105</lpage></element-citation></ref><ref id="b21-ehp0115-000743"><element-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group><name><surname>Morello-Frosch</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name><name><surname>Jesdale</surname><given-names>BM</given-names></name></person-group><year>2006</year><article-title>Separate and unequal: residential segregation and estimated cancer risks associated with ambient air toxics in U.S. metropolitan areas</article-title><source>Envi